WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.210 --> 00:00:01.200
- And what about fracking-

00:00:01.200 --> 00:00:02.240
- He's trying to respond.

00:00:02.240 --> 00:00:04.680
- I've never said I oppose fracking.

00:00:04.680 --> 00:00:06.310
- He'll be against it very soon because

00:00:06.310 --> 00:00:09.360
his party is totally against it.

00:00:09.360 --> 00:00:11.370
- [Narrator] Natural gas extraction by way

00:00:11.370 --> 00:00:14.700
of hydraulic fracturing or
fracking may not have been

00:00:14.700 --> 00:00:17.180
the top issue on the minds
of most voters coming

00:00:17.180 --> 00:00:18.860
into this election season.

00:00:18.860 --> 00:00:20.660
But in the final weeks of the campaign,

00:00:20.660 --> 00:00:23.193
they've witnessed a
frack is over fracking.

00:00:24.290 --> 00:00:26.460
- You yourself said on multiple occasions

00:00:26.460 --> 00:00:28.480
when you were running for president

00:00:28.480 --> 00:00:29.970
that you would ban fracking.

00:00:29.970 --> 00:00:32.630
- Joe Biden will not ban fracking.

00:00:32.630 --> 00:00:34.360
That is a fact.

00:00:34.360 --> 00:00:37.300
- [Narrator] So why so
much talk of fracking?

00:00:37.300 --> 00:00:39.970
Because Pennsylvania is
the biggest swing state

00:00:39.970 --> 00:00:43.040
after Florida and
fracking could be the key

00:00:43.040 --> 00:00:44.710
to the Keystone State.

00:00:44.710 --> 00:00:48.370
In 2016, Trump won the state
by running up the score

00:00:48.370 --> 00:00:51.793
in blue collar counties
like those round Pittsburgh.

00:00:52.850 --> 00:00:56.300
- To all the people of
Pennsylvania here this morning

00:00:56.300 --> 00:01:00.840
if Biden's elected, he will
wipe out your energy industry.

00:01:00.840 --> 00:01:05.540
- I am not, not, not
banning fracking period.

00:01:05.540 --> 00:01:07.490
- [Narrator] Pittsburgh and
its surrounding counties used

00:01:07.490 --> 00:01:11.000
to be united in a kind of
iron triangle of steel,

00:01:11.000 --> 00:01:13.520
labor unions, and democratic politics

00:01:13.520 --> 00:01:16.400
but steel and coal entered along decline

00:01:16.400 --> 00:01:19.820
then fracking brought
new jobs, income and hope

00:01:19.820 --> 00:01:22.030
to counties outside of Pittsburgh

00:01:22.030 --> 00:01:25.550
which had become more republican
while Pittsburgh has turned

00:01:25.550 --> 00:01:28.930
to tech and remained solidly democrat.

00:01:28.930 --> 00:01:31.550
When the fracking boom
took off in Pennsylvania,

00:01:31.550 --> 00:01:34.770
so did employment jobs and
two major components of oil

00:01:34.770 --> 00:01:37.370
and gas extraction grew fourfold.

00:01:37.370 --> 00:01:41.520
- What really made our company
grow was when we started

00:01:41.520 --> 00:01:44.370
to support the oil and gas industry.

00:01:44.370 --> 00:01:46.360
- [Narrator] Paul Bergad
owns a small business

00:01:46.360 --> 00:01:48.660
that manufacturers foam products used by

00:01:48.660 --> 00:01:50.230
the fracking industry.

00:01:50.230 --> 00:01:52.880
Bergad lives and works
in Armstrong County,

00:01:52.880 --> 00:01:54.410
just Northeast of Pittsburgh.

00:01:54.410 --> 00:01:58.830
- In an area where we had
people leaving in mass Exodus,

00:01:58.830 --> 00:02:01.380
it's the oil and gas that's
bringing people back.

00:02:01.380 --> 00:02:03.920
It is the new steel mill.

00:02:03.920 --> 00:02:07.480
Everybody knows somebody
that's in that industry.

00:02:07.480 --> 00:02:09.740
- [Narrator] But in recent
years the US fracking industry

00:02:09.740 --> 00:02:12.730
has essentially become a
victim of its own success.

00:02:12.730 --> 00:02:15.480
Pumping so much gas that excess supply

00:02:15.480 --> 00:02:18.690
has kept prices depressed
and here that's led

00:02:18.690 --> 00:02:20.680
to less jobs in fracking.

00:02:20.680 --> 00:02:23.230
According to data by the
US Commerce Department

00:02:23.230 --> 00:02:26.700
by late 2019 employment
in the two big components

00:02:26.700 --> 00:02:29.900
of Pennsylvania's oil
and gas sector had fallen

00:02:29.900 --> 00:02:31.790
by about 26%.

00:02:31.790 --> 00:02:33.560
- If we lose that oil and gas industry,

00:02:33.560 --> 00:02:38.320
that is what pays the overhead,
is what pays the labor

00:02:38.320 --> 00:02:41.963
and when you begin to take
something like that away,

00:02:43.040 --> 00:02:47.340
the business may not be
profitable enough to survive.

00:02:47.340 --> 00:02:51.290
- I see us reverting back
to a desperate situation

00:02:51.290 --> 00:02:53.140
that we were before we
had the industry here

00:02:53.140 --> 00:02:54.890
in Western Pennsylvania.

00:02:54.890 --> 00:02:57.080
- [Narrator] Jen McIntyre
works as a consultant

00:02:57.080 --> 00:02:58.320
for the fracking industry.

00:02:58.320 --> 00:03:01.510
She lives and in Washington
County, South of Pittsburgh.

00:03:01.510 --> 00:03:05.110
- It's the difference between
us being gainfully employed

00:03:05.110 --> 00:03:05.990
or not employed?

00:03:05.990 --> 00:03:08.985
My husband doesn't have
a degree to fall back on.

00:03:08.985 --> 00:03:11.350
- Bergad and McIntyre say they both voted

00:03:11.350 --> 00:03:14.850
for Trump last time and
plan to do so again.

00:03:14.850 --> 00:03:17.700
One reason on the issue
of fracking they say

00:03:17.700 --> 00:03:20.860
they don't trust Biden and the democrats.

00:03:20.860 --> 00:03:23.000
- No more, no, no fracking.

00:03:23.000 --> 00:03:24.590
- [Narrator] After a
March democratic debate

00:03:24.590 --> 00:03:27.290
Biden's campaign clarified
that his position proposes

00:03:27.290 --> 00:03:30.913
a ban only on new
fracking on federal lands.

00:03:32.020 --> 00:03:34.660
While people in McIntyre's
community make their living

00:03:34.660 --> 00:03:36.830
from the drilling economy,

00:03:36.830 --> 00:03:39.220
a short distance away, a
growing number of workers

00:03:39.220 --> 00:03:42.560
are part of the coding
economy in Pittsburgh

00:03:42.560 --> 00:03:46.360
at companies like Google,
Tesla and Duolingo.

00:03:46.360 --> 00:03:50.440
High-tech jobs now account for
roughly 24% of the workforce

00:03:50.440 --> 00:03:51.970
in and around the city according

00:03:51.970 --> 00:03:54.280
to the Pittsburgh technology council.

00:03:54.280 --> 00:03:56.299
- We have a lot of great universities

00:03:56.299 --> 00:03:59.900
and big tech companies,
but also a strong heritage

00:03:59.900 --> 00:04:02.783
of steel working and factory
working in middle-class.

00:04:04.690 --> 00:04:07.200
- [Narrator] Todd Medema moved
from California to Pittsburgh

00:04:07.200 --> 00:04:10.570
about 10 years ago to study
at Carnegie Mellon university.

00:04:10.570 --> 00:04:13.050
After graduating he stayed to work

00:04:13.050 --> 00:04:15.940
for Uber self-driving vehicle program.

00:04:15.940 --> 00:04:17.500
Medema recently switched to another

00:04:17.500 --> 00:04:19.070
high-tech transportation company.

00:04:19.070 --> 00:04:22.300
- So Google moving to
Pittsburgh back in 2005, 2006,

00:04:22.300 --> 00:04:25.170
really kicked off a flywheel
effect where instead

00:04:25.170 --> 00:04:27.240
of everyone leaving Pittsburgh,

00:04:27.240 --> 00:04:29.520
they would stay, start new companies

00:04:29.520 --> 00:04:32.280
and now we have a thriving startup scene,

00:04:32.280 --> 00:04:33.520
multiple incubators.

00:04:33.520 --> 00:04:35.390
- [Narrator] Most of these
tech workers hold bachelor's

00:04:35.390 --> 00:04:38.430
or advanced degrees, these
types of voters have been

00:04:38.430 --> 00:04:39.874
swinging away from the GOP.

00:04:39.874 --> 00:04:42.610
- For the 2020 presidential election,

00:04:42.610 --> 00:04:44.510
my top issue is the environment

00:04:44.510 --> 00:04:48.070
and especially having a strong plan

00:04:48.070 --> 00:04:49.217
to address climate change.

00:04:49.217 --> 00:04:51.610
- [Narrator] Opponents of
fracking say it prolongs

00:04:51.610 --> 00:04:54.400
the country's reliance on fossil fuels.

00:04:54.400 --> 00:04:57.600
It's also become controversial
because of chemicals used

00:04:57.600 --> 00:05:00.010
in the process that
could take water supplies

00:05:00.010 --> 00:05:02.200
if not handled properly.

00:05:02.200 --> 00:05:05.750
Despite fracking's downsides
Medema says he understands

00:05:05.750 --> 00:05:09.590
his fellow Pennsylvania's
fears about losing jobs.

00:05:09.590 --> 00:05:11.030
- People who work on the fracking

00:05:11.030 --> 00:05:14.630
are honest hardworking Americans

00:05:14.630 --> 00:05:18.113
and I really have no fault with them.

00:05:19.070 --> 00:05:21.610
If you really want good
jobs, you'll vote for Biden

00:05:21.610 --> 00:05:23.340
because he has a plan to make

00:05:23.340 --> 00:05:27.800
the American economy
innovative and relevant

00:05:27.800 --> 00:05:31.210
going forward not just for
today's fossil fuel industry.

00:05:31.210 --> 00:05:33.730
- [Narrator] But voters like
Bergard are not convinced.

00:05:33.730 --> 00:05:37.000
- When they talk about the
new jobs that will come

00:05:37.000 --> 00:05:42.000
with solar, with windmills
the other energies,

00:05:42.320 --> 00:05:45.820
there's nothing there that says for sure

00:05:45.820 --> 00:05:47.230
that is gonna happen.

00:05:47.230 --> 00:05:49.270
- [Narrator] On election
day, it could all come down

00:05:49.270 --> 00:05:51.976
to what happens in Western Pennsylvania.

00:05:51.976 --> 00:05:54.930
- Eight days from now we're
going to win the Commonwealth

00:05:54.930 --> 00:05:56.290
of Pennsylvania.

00:05:56.290 --> 00:05:58.570
- [Narrator] Biden hopes
to hold on to progressives

00:05:58.570 --> 00:06:01.180
while peeling off some of
the pro-fracking voters

00:06:01.180 --> 00:06:02.840
who went for Trump last time

00:06:02.840 --> 00:06:05.810
and Trump needs more
pro-fracking blue collar workers

00:06:05.810 --> 00:06:10.270
from this area casting ballots
for him than did in 2016.

00:06:10.270 --> 00:06:14.730
Two groups, so geographically
close yet politically,

00:06:14.730 --> 00:06:16.475
so far away.

00:06:16.475 --> 00:06:18.892
(soft music)

